main.py
--unwind 5

^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
convert_with (python_converter_except.cpp) calls __enter__ but never
emits the __exit__ call. A bug inside __exit__ is never checked and
exception suppression is not modeled. Fix: after the with-body, emit
__exit__(mgr, None, None, None); to model suppression, clear
__exception_active when __exit__ returns True and an exception is active.
